      "text": "The factor is the average of the two High-prior-return portfolios minus the average of the two Low-prior-return portfolios, using the value-weighted returns from the first (Average Value Weighted Returns, Monthly) table. The script reads only that block, treats -99.99 and -999 as missing, and skips any month where a needed portfolio is missing.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport math\nimport csv\n\nINPUT = \"6_Portfolios_ME_Prior_12_2.csv\"\nOUTPUT = \"output.csv\"\n\n\ndef parse_monthly_value_weighted(path):\n    \"\"\"Parse the first monthly block (Average Value Weighted Returns -- Monthly).\n\n    Column order in the file:\n      0: SMALL LoPRIOR, 1: ME1 PRIOR2, 2: SMALL HiPRIOR,\n      3: BIG LoPRIOR,   4: ME2 PRIOR2, 5: BIG HiPRIOR\n    \"\"\"\n    rows = []\n    started = False\n    date_re = re.compile(r\"\\d{6}\")\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"latin-1\", errors=\"ignore\") as f:\n        for line in f:\n            parts = [p.strip() for p in line.strip().split(\",\")]\n            if len(parts) == 7 and date_re.fullmatch(parts[0]):\n                started = True\n                vals = []\n                for p in parts[1:]:\n                    try:\n                        v = float(p)\n                    except ValueError:\n                        v = math.nan\n                    if v == -99.99 or v == -999.0:\n                        v = math.nan\n                    vals.append(v)\n                rows.append((int(parts[0]), vals))\n            elif started:\n                # first monthly block ended (blank line / next section / footer)\n                break\n    return rows\n\n\ndef main():\n    rows = parse_monthly_value_weighted(INPUT)\n\n    # Dedupe by date (keep first occurrence) and sort\n    seen = {}\n    for d, vals in rows:\n        if d not in seen:\n            seen[d] = vals\n    dates = sorted(seen)\n\n    out = []\n    for d in dates:\n        v = seen[d]\n        small_lo, small_hi = v[0], v[2]\n        big_lo, big_hi = v[3], v[5]\n        needed = [small_lo, small_hi, big_lo, big_hi]\n        if any(math.isnan(x) for x in needed):\n            continue\n        mom = 0.5 * (small_hi + big_hi) - 0.5 * (small_lo + big_lo)\n        out.append((d, mom))\n\n    with open(OUTPUT, \"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"date\", \"value\"])\n        for d, m in out:\n            w.writerow([d, repr(float(m))])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
